  "details": "I would like something like SourceBans in TF2.\n\nWe have a database of banned, muted, or gagged (no chat) players and the duration of their punishment.\n\nThe database of punishments has a web interface so they can be viewed with the reason and what admin issued the ban. \n\nThis page acts as an administrative tool, a verbose moderator audit log, and a page for users to review why they were punished and reach out to appeal if that community offers it.\n\nThe current Groups ban-list just lists everyone's profile with a huge profile image. There are no ban durations. There is no logged ban reason. There is no way for normal members to review it. There are audit logs but it's a bit clunky.\n\nAs an example, here is Skial community's actual SourceBan page.\n\nhttps://www.skial.com/sourcebans/\n\nIf you'd like to browse the source code for SourceBans++ (current version most Source servers use), you can find it here:\n\nhttps://github.com/sbpp/sourcebans-pp",
